<title>UK: Status Quo falls victim to French drivers' strike.</title>
<headline>Status Quo falls victim to French drivers' strike.</headline>
<dateline>BELFAST 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The &quot;Can't Stop&quot; tour of veteran British rock band Status Quo ground to a halt on Tuesday because their equipment is stuck in the French truck drivers' strike.</p>
<p>The band had three concerts scheduled in Northern Ireland this week, but its gear, in two 45-foot trucks, is not expected to arrive until Saturday, a Status Quo spokesman said.</p>
<p>The members of the band, all in their 40s and 50s, are in Northern Ireland. But the spokesman said; &quot;They've two truck loads full of lights, guitars and stage stuff and it's all stuck there.&quot;</p>
</text>
